39800a010643e46da34385b9194a496377f6daecec0ececea1aa\", \"4cee1d240e8ab206cd7d74c19b4719e4408a07b635c680c4dbb35d8fcff98c17\", \"4778b54477859cea6c865d619133d1d08761b47fcb4fb42f4f3dfa0b61dbcbfc\", \"eebb0542e89f5f5f053fd8a284697832a10140009fd2667c0ab0f075192cd052\"],\n  \"reviewerType\": \"llm-vision-headless-cli\",\n  \"summary\": \"Across 21 Cedar Commons HOA screens, the same five-row block — Property / Record / History / Owner inbox / Change option — is rendered verbatim on at least 12 screens, and its body text is disjunctive placeholder copy rather than the record actually on screen (e.g. 'Community Rules, Room A reservation, dues receipt, or architectural case' appears on the dues payment, fence request, committee decision, and room reservation screens alike). Most descriptive text is written as capability spec rather than product copy — sentences ending in 'are visible', 'remain visible', 'match the state' — so a homeowner reading these screens learns what the app can display, not what their own reservation, dues bill, or fence request says. Several screens also show cross-workflow bleed: the facility-reservation action sheet asks the user to 'Choose attendance … Going, Maybe, or Not going' for a clubhouse room booking, the dues-payment start screen surfaces a 'Facility reservation a…' card, and the member-document start screen surfaces an 'HOA export' card. Only the owner-notification trio carries genuinely specific copy ('Your slate gray fence repaint is approved if trim remains cedar and work starts within 30 days', 'Send today at 4:15 PM'), which proves the bar the other five workflows fall short of; the review fails.\",\n  \"holisticQuestionAnswers\": [\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"context-state-legibility\",\n      \"question\": \"Across this community's workflows, is it always clear what workflow and what state (start/in-progress/complete) the user is looking at?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Partially. The action and complete states are usually legible — action sheets carry a specific modal title ('Clubhouse Room A reservation', 'Fence color request', 'Quarterly HOA dues', 'HOA records export', 'Community Rules document', 'Send owner notice'), and complete screens carry an explicit terminal banner ('HOA record saved', 'Request outcome saved', 'Owner notified', 'Member result'). The start states are much weaker: five of seven open mid-scroll under the generic 'Cedar Commons HOA' app bar with no workflow title in view, so the facility-reservation start screen leads with a clipped 'Cedar Commons / Receipt/audit' chip row and a 'Response choices' card, and the architectural-request start screen leads with a half-cut line reading 'Commons HOA; sender is the HOA board.' Worse, the workflow identity on several start screens contradicts the row: the dues-payment start screen's only titled card is 'Facility reservation a…', and the member-document start screen's only titled card is 'HOA export'. A 'Waiting' pill appears on the export, architectural-request, and member-document starts without saying what is being waited on.\",\n      \"score\": 48,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"On cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-dues-payment-start the only card title visible is 'Facility reservation a…' with a 'Reserve and pay' button, not a dues-payment surface\",\n        \"On cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-member-document-start the foreground card reads 'HOA export' / 'You can read the current details without changing …' rather than a Community Rules document\",\n        \"On cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-architectural-request-start the topmost visible text is the clipped fragment 'Commons HOA; sender is the HOA board.' with no workflow heading on screen\",\n        \"On cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-export-evidence-start a bare 'Waiting' pill sits at the right edge with no adjacent text explaining what is pending\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-export-evidence-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-architectural-request-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-dues-payment-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-committee-decision-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-member-document-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-owner-notification-start\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"copy-accuracy\",\n      \"question\": \"Does the displayed text read as real product copy describing actual Cedar Commons HOA content, or as generic template/spec filler?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Mostly spec filler. The recurring 'Record' row lists four unrelated record types joined by 'or' — 'Community Rules, Room A reservation, dues receipt, or architectural case' — on screens where exactly one of those is the subject, which is template text that was never resolved to the instance. The same is true of 'Change option: Cancel reservation, request changes, retry payment, or reopen where policy allows', shown identically on a document view and a payment. Section bodies are written from the capability spec's point of view: 'Payer, amount, privacy choice, entitlement, receipt destination, and retry/refund options are visible', 'Labeled fields, privacy indicators, attachments, assignee, and status are visible', 'Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible'. These describe the UI instead of showing the data — the dues screens never show a dollar amount, the export screens never show a file size or checksum value, and the reservation screens never show a date or time slot. The owner-notification and architectural-request screens are the exceptions with real specifics: 'Lot 42 fence repaint, slate gray, decision due Friday' and 'Your slate gray fence repaint is approved if trim remains cedar and work starts within 30 days.'\",\n      \"score\": 30,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"'Community Rules, Room A reservation, dues receipt, or architectural case.' renders under 'Record' on the dues, fence-request, committee-decision and room-reservation screens alike\",\n        \"'Payer, amount, privacy choice, entitlement, receipt destination, and retry/refund options are visible.' is shown in place of an actual dues amount on the dues-payment action sheet\",\n        \"'Scope, redaction, checksum, destination, transfer status, rollback, and audit evidence are visible.' appears under 'Export workspace' with no scope, checksum or destination value rendered\",\n        \"By contrast the owner-notification screens show 'Send today at 4:15 PM to owner inbox and email receipt.' — a concrete, instance-level fact\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-complete\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-export-evidence-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-export-evidence-complete\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-architectural-request-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-dues-payment-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-dues-payment-complete\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-committee-decision-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-committee-decision-complete\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"visual-repetition\",\n      \"question\": \"Do the screens avoid repeated generic card shells and thin/empty content where real content is expected?\",\n      \"answer\": \"No. The identical five-row icon list (house/Property, page/Record, clock/History, tray/Owner inbox, undo/Change option) is the dominant visual unit on at least twelve of the twenty-one screens, appearing as 'Event details', 'Export steps', 'Decision queue', 'Payment summary', 'Submitted details', and 'Submitted request' — six different headings over one identical body. Two screens duplicate the block within a single scroll: the facility-reservation action sheet shows 'Event details / Property / Lot 42, homeowner Avery Brooks…' at the top and again inside 'Choose attendance' at the bottom, and the owner-notification action sheet shows 'Sender and recipient / Message body' twice, once under 'Notice preview' and again under 'Delivery actions'. The export-evidence and member-document start screens both end in roughly 500px of empty dark canvas below a collapsed 'Local package details' row. Chip rows ('Cedar Commons', 'Receipt/audit', 'Documents', 'Availability', 'Outcome history') repeat verbatim across workflows and are visually indistinguishable from each other.\",\n      \"score\": 27,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"The same Property/Record/History/Owner inbox/Change option list appears under 'Event details', 'Export steps', 'Decision queue', 'Payment summary' and 'Submitted details' headings\",\n        \"On cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-action the row 'Property — Lot 42, homeowner Avery Brooks, Cedar Commons' renders twice in one scroll view\",\n        \"On cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-owner-notification-action 'Sender and recipient' + 'Message body' repeat verbatim under both 'Notice preview' and 'Delivery actions'\",\n        \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-export-evidence-start and -member-document-start both leave a large blank region under the collapsed 'Local package details' disclosure\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-complete\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-export-evidence-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-export-evidence-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-architectural-request-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-architectural-request-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-architectural-request-complete\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-dues-payment-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-dues-payment-complete\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-committee-decision-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-committee-decision-complete\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-member-document-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-own