al-request-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-dues-payment-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-committee-decision-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-member-document-start\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"questionId\": \"workflow-scoping-correctness\",\n      \"question\": \"Does the content shown on each screen make sense for the workflow being demonstrated?\",\n      \"answer\": \"Not consistently. The clearest defect is the facility-reservation action sheet titled 'Clubhouse Room A reservation' whose main interactive card is 'Choose attendance — Event date, capacity, location, host note, and reminders are visible before choosing Going, Maybe, or Not going', with an 'Attendance options: Going, Maybe, Not going, and Change response remain available while the event is open' row. That is an RSVP-to-an-event model applied to booking a room; a homeowner reserving Room A does not RSVP to their own booking. Beyond that, the dues-payment start screen's foreground card is a facility-reservation card, the member-document start screen's foreground card is an HOA export card, the facility-reservation start screen's foreground card is 'Architectural request' with a 'Submit request' button, and the committee-decision start screen's foreground card is 'Member-visible docu…' with 'Waiting for the member form to be submitted.' In each case the state being demonstrated belongs to a different workflow than the row claims.\",\n      \"score\": 33,\n      \"blocksPass\": true,\n      \"visibleEvidence\": [\n        \"'Choose attendance … before choosing Going, Maybe, or Not going' appears under the title 'Clubhouse Room A reservation'\",\n        \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-start foregrounds an 'Architectural request' card with a 'Submit request' button\",\n        \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-committee-decision-start foregrounds 'Member-visible docu…' / 'Waiting for the member form to be submitted.'\",\n        \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-dues-payment-start foregrounds 'Facility reservation a…' with 'Payment details' and 'Reserve and pay'\"\n      ],\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-action\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-dues-payment-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-committee-decision-start\", \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-member-document-start\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"screenReviews\": [\n    {\n      \"screenRowId\": \"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-start\",\n      \"affectedScreenRowIds\": [\"cedar-commons-hoa-hoa-facility-reservation-start\"],\n      \"critique\": \"This is supposed to be the start of a clubhouse facility reservation, but the screen opens mid-scroll with the chip row 'Cedar Commons / Receipt/audit' clipped by the app bar, and the single most prominent card below the fold is 'Architectural request — Submitted details are ready for a decision and …' with a 'Submit request' button. The reservation affordance that does exist, 'Reserve and pay', sits inside a pale translucent card headed 'Response choices' whose body — 'Confirm the amount or scope, change details, retry if needed, and keep the receipt or export progress visible.' — is capability prose, not a description of any room, date, or fee. Nothing on screen names the facility being reserved.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"fail\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"targetProductionSurface\": \"A reservation entry point that names the facility (Clubhouse Room A), shows the requested date/time slot, current availability, and the reservation fee, with 'Reserve and pay' as the single obvious primary action and no unrelated architectural-request card competing for the foreground.\",\n      \"visibleObservations\": [\"App bar 'Cedar Commons HOA' with bell, chat, and people icons\", \"Clipped chip row 'Cedar Commons' / 'Receipt/audit' cut by the app bar\", \"'Response choices' card: 'Confirm the amount or scope, change details, retry if needed, and keep the receipt or export progress visible